🧠 Reviewer openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna enters the chamber...
  ✓ CONFIRMED: Reward reinvestment is vulnerable to spot-price sandwich man
    Justification: Upon reviewing RewardReinvestor.splitReinvest() in 
src/contracts/RewardReinvestor.sol and UniswapHandler.buyMalt() in 
src/contracts/DexHandlers/UniswapHandler.sol, I confirmed the alleged spot-price
manipulation vulnerability. splitReinvest() withdraws rewards, transfers half to
the handler, and invokes buyMalt() without accepting or propagating any 
user-supplied minimum Malt output or deadline. buyMalt() computes the complete 
reward balance and calls router.swapExactTokensForTokens() with amountOutMin set
to 0 and deadline set only to now. Consequently, an attacker can front-run a 
pending reinvestment transaction by moving the reward/Malt Uniswap reserves, 
cause the swap to execute at an unfavorable but non-reverting rate, and reverse 
the reserve manipulation afterward. The subsequent _bondAccount() flow does not 
validate the purchased Malt amount against an expected price; its addLiquidity()
call only applies a 95% balance-based minimum and is not a reliable protection 
against a modest sandwich. The same zero-output protection also exists in 
sellMalt(), although it is not required for this attack. No relevant oracle or 
TWAP guard is used in the reinvestment path.


